      ],
      timeline: [
        '1235: Poetry anthology compiled.',
        "16th Century: Portuguese 'Carta' (cards) arrive and merge with Japanese shell-matching traditions.",
        '1904: Official competitive Karuta rules established.',
        'Present: A massive cultural event in Japan, with national tournaments held at the Omi Jingu shrine.',
      ],
      evolution: 'Originally a literary game for nobility, it evolved into a highly athletic sport requiring split-second physical reactions.',
