          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Empty your territory of cards before your opponent.',
          gameplay: "1. A reader ('Yomite') reads the first half (upper phrase) of a poem.\n2. Both players attempt to touch the grabbing card containing the second half (lower phrase).\n3. If you grab a card in your own territory, it is removed.\n4. If you grab a card in your opponent's territory, you send one card from your territory to theirs.\n5. **Otetsuki (Fault)**: Touching the wrong card results in a penalty (opponent sends a card).",
          keyRules: [
            'Reader recites the first phrase of a poem; first to touch the matching Torifuda wins that card. Correct touch in your territory removes the card; correct touch in opponent territory lets you send one card from your territory to theirs. Wrong touch (otetsuki) gives the opponent a card. First to empty their territory wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Memorize the first few syllables ('Kimari-ji') of each poem. Many poems can be identified after just 1, 2, or 3 syllables.",
          intermediate: 'Territory management: Group poems with similar starting sounds together so your hand is already in the right area when the reader begins.',
          advanced: 'Defensive posture: Position cards you are less confident in at the edges of your territory to make them harder for the opponent to steal.',
          tips: [
            "Speed is secondary to accuracy; a 'fault' is more costly than being slightly slower.",
            'Listen for the specific pitch and rhythm of the reader, as it can precede the actual words.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
