          deckDescription: 'The Hyakunin Isshu (One Hundred Poets) karuta set: 200 cards total. One hundred Yomifuda (reading cards) show the first half of each poem; one hundred Torifuda (grabbing cards) show the second half. In competitive play, 50 Torifuda are used (25 per player); the reader reads from the Yomifuda.',
          suitDescription: "There are no traditional suits; the 100 poems are the organizing principle. Each poem has a unique reading card and a unique grabbing card; players match the read phrase to the correct grabbing card by touch. Cards are grouped by territory (yours vs opponent's) on the floor.",
          rankDescription: 'Cards have no numeric rank; each of the 100 poems has one Yomifuda and one Torifuda. The reader recites the first phrase; the matching Torifuda is the only correct card to touch. Speed and accuracy in matching determine who removes the card or sends a card to the opponent.',
          dealPattern: 'Shuffle 100 Torifuda; each player receives 25 cards for their territory (face-up on mat). Remaining 50 Torifuda are not used this round. Reader holds the 100 Yomifuda (reading deck).',
